---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import EvidenceStrip from "../../components/EvidenceStrip.astro";
import MeetingFlow from "../../components/MeetingFlow.astro";
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";

const project = projects.find((p) => p.id === "notetaker")!;
---

<Base
  title="Notetaker, Jamal Mammadzada"
  description="A case study on a consent-first native macOS app that captures meeting audio, transcribes on-device, and writes structured Markdown notes."
  progress={true}
>
  <article>
    <header class="wrap case-head">
      <p class="mono"><a href="/work/">Work</a> / Case study {project.index}</p>
      <h1 class="h-xl case-title">Notetaker</h1>
      <p class="lede narrow case-lede">
        A native macOS menu-bar app that records the meeting you explicitly
        approve, transcribes it on-device, and leaves behind notes you can edit.
        Its most important feature is the recording it refuses to start by itself.
      </p>

      <dl class="meta-grid case-meta">
        {project.meta.map((m) => <div><dt>{m.label}</dt><dd>{m.value}</dd></div>)}
        <div><dt>Built</dt><dd>{project.years}</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <p class="note case-note">
        The repository is private. This case study documents the architecture,
        privacy boundary, and verified behavior without publishing meeting data,
        prompts, credentials, or private source.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap case-proof">
      <EvidenceStrip
        label="Notetaker evidence"
        items={[
          { value: "2 signals", label: "Zoom detection", detail: "Helper process plus window title" },
          { value: "16 kHz", label: "Local audio", detail: "System and microphone mixed to mono WAV" },
          { value: "1 text pass", label: "Summarization", detail: "No audio leaves the machine" },
          { value: "3 harnesses", label: "Focused checks", detail: "Detection, title safety, and WAV output" },
        ]}
      />
    </div>

    <section class="wrap section narrow" aria-labelledby="boundary-first">
      <h2 class="h-lg sec-title" id="boundary-first">The boundary comes first</h2>
      <p>
        Meeting automation has an unusually sharp failure mode: convenience can
        become silent recording. Notetaker treats detection and consent as two
        different events. Seeing Zoom's in-meeting helper process or a live
        meeting title is enough to show a prompt. It is never enough to begin capture.
      </p>
      <p>
        That distinction survives the whole design. Audio stays on the Mac.
        whisper.cpp produces a local transcript. Only after recording stops does
        a single text-only request turn that transcript into decisions and action
        items. The editable Markdown result stays beside the source transcript.
      </p>

      <MeetingFlow />
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="system-shape">
      <h2 class="h-lg sec-title narrow" id="system-shape">A small app with a real pipeline</h2>
      <div class="architecture">
        <div class="arch-card reveal">
          <p class="mono">Capture</p>
          <h3 class="h-sm">ScreenCaptureKit</h3>
          <p>
            The stream combines system audio—the people on the other side—with
            microphone input. A discarded 2×2 pixel region satisfies the capture
            API without turning the app into a screen recorder.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-card reveal">
          <p class="mono">Normalize</p>
          <h3 class="h-sm">WAVWriter</h3>
          <p>
            Audio is converted to 16 kHz mono WAV so the transcription stage gets
            one predictable format regardless of the devices active in the meeting.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-card reveal">
          <p class="mono">Understand</p>
          <h3 class="h-sm">whisper.cpp → Markdown</h3>
          <p>
            Transcription runs locally. A meeting topic, sanitized before it can
            become a folder name, gives the final summarizer enough context to
            produce a useful heading and clearer notes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section narrow" aria-labelledby="verified">
      <h2 class="h-lg sec-title" id="verified">The bugs that looked like success</h2>
      <p>
        Audio software can return a valid file while recording the wrong thing.
        One ScreenCaptureKit flag produced exactly that failure: the WAV looked
        normal but system-audio amplitude dropped to zero, leaving only the
        microphone. The repository keeps a focused WAV harness because checking
        that a file exists would have passed.
      </p>

      <div class="checks">
        <div><span class="mono">01 · Capture</span><p>Inspect the output structure and measured signal, not just file creation.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">02 · Detection</span><p>Exercise the meeting signal separately from the permission to record.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">03 · Titles</span><p>Test slashes, colons, and newlines before calendar text becomes a path.</p></div>
      </div>

      <details class="tech">
        <summary>What the app deliberately does not guess</summary>
        <p>
          whisper.cpp does not provide reliable speaker diarization here, so the
          note prompt only attributes a statement when context makes the speaker
          clear. A missing label is more honest than a polished wrong one.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap section narrow" aria-labelledby="limits">
      <h2 class="h-lg sec-title" id="limits">What remains unsolved</h2>
      <p>
        This is a useful personal tool, not a general meeting platform. Rebuilding
        the app can cause macOS to ask for capture permission again because the
        code identity changes. Transcription speed and quality depend on the local
        model and the audio. Participant names are unavailable without adding a
        Zoom cloud integration, which would create a much larger privacy and
        authentication surface than this app currently needs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="wrap section case-next" aria-label="More work">
      <a href="/work/frcmob/" class="next-link">
        <span class="mono">Back to the first case study</span>
        <span class="h-md">FRCMOB →</span>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-head { padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); }
  .case-head > .mono { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .case-title { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .case-lede { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .case-meta { max-width: 38rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .case-note { max-width: 62ch; }
  .case-proof { margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); }
  .sec-title { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

  .architecture {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .arch-card { background: var(--paper-2); padding: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.6rem); }
  .arch-card .mono { color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .arch-card h3 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .arch-card p:last-child { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .checks { display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; margin: 1.7rem 0; }
  .checks > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 0.8rem; }
  .checks .mono { color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.62rem; }
  .checks p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .case-next { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .next-link { display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; padding: 1.5rem 0; }
  .next-link .h-md { transition: color 0.16s ease; }
  .next-link:hover .h-md { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .architecture { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .checks > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.35rem; }
  }
</style>
